>>
Rule 1 (Input tensor and other tensor must have broadcastable shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 2 (Output tensor must be of boolean type)
{v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = 0
>>
Rule 3 (Input tensor must not be complex double)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 13 (Input tensor must not be complex double to avoid 'ge_cpu' error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 17 (If out is provided its shape must match the broadcasted shape of input and other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |=  ndim(v_3) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3,i)) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_3,i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 21 (If output tensor provided, then it should have correct dimension with respect to input tensor, other tensor, and they are broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) > 0 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : (i < ndim(v_3)) ∧ ((i >= ndim(v_1) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1)-1-i) = shape(v_3, ndim(v_3) -1 -i) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1)-1-i) = 1) ∧ (i >= ndim(v_2) ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2)-1-i) = shape(v_3, ndim(v_3) -1 -i) ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2)-1-i) = 1)))
>>
Rule 22 (Input and other tensors should not have string type as it does not support ge_cpu operation)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 43 (If other is a tensor, it can't be of string type.)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 57 (Input, other, and out must all be the same numerical type if out is provided and input and other are tensors.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8) ∧ (dtype_(v_3) ≤ 8) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_3)
